

**Orthogonal Polynomials as Confluent Hypergeometric Functions (see chapter 13)**

\[\begin{array}{lcl}22.5.54&L_{s}^{(a)}(x)=\binom{n+a}{n}M(-n,\alpha+1,\,x)\\ &&\\ &\textbf{Orthogonal Polynomials as Parabolic Cylinder Functions (see chapter 19)}&\\ &&\\ 22.5.55&H_{n}(x)=2^{n}U\left(\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{2}\,n,\frac{3}{2}\,x^{2} \right)\\ &&\\ 22.5.56&H_{2m}(x)=(-1)^{m}\frac{(2m)!}{m!}M\left(-m,\frac{1}{2}\,x^{2}\right) \\ &&\\ 22.5.57&H_{2m+1}(x)=(-1)^{m}\,\frac{(2m+1)!}{m!}\,2M\left(-m,\frac{3}{2},x^{2} \right)\\ &&\\ \end{array}\]

\[\begin{array}{lcl}22.5.58&H_{n}(x)=2^{n/2}e^{2^{n/2}}D_{n}(\sqrt{2}x)=2^{n/2} e^{2^{n/2}}U\left(-n-\frac{1}{2}\,\sqrt{2}x\right)\\ &&\\ 22.5.59&He_{n}(x)=e^{2^{n/2}}D_{n}(x)=e^{2^{n/2}}U\left(-n-\frac{1}{2}\,x\right) \\ &&\\ &\textbf{Orthogonal Polynomials as Legendre Functions (see chapter 8)}&\\ &&\\ 22.5.60&C_{n}^{(a)}(x)=\\ &&\\ &\frac{\Gamma(\alpha+\frac{1}{2})\,\Gamma(2\alpha+n)}{n!\Gamma(2\alpha)}\left[ \frac{1}{4}\,(x^{2}-1)\right]^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}}P_{n+m-1}^{(A-\alpha)}(x)\\ &&\\ &(\alpha\neq 0)\\ &&\\ \end{array}\]